            "en": {
              "mode": "text",
              "body": "A predicative universe forms objects using data from previously available or lower universes; quantifying over a universe generally raises the result to a higher universe. An impredicative sort permits a definition to quantify over a collection that already contains the result sort itself. This is a formation principle: it does not by itself imply proof irrelevance, classical logic, or unrestricted elimination into data-bearing universes.",
